README.md:1:Synthetic application fixture. No framework, database server, provider account or running application is installed. Source contracts are examples for read-only routing/planning, not evidence of production behavior.
contracts/provider.md:1:# Synthetic payment/SMS provider contract
contracts/provider.md:2:No network calls are authorized. POST /payments accepts a stable Idempotency-Key per business operation; repeated keys return the same operation. A timeout does not prove failure: query GET /payments/by-key before a new payment. HTTP 429 supplies Retry-After seconds or HTTP-date; honor its bounded delay and provider quota. Retry only documented transient failures with a finite budget. Webhooks carry event_id, resource_id, version, state and a timestamped HMAC signature over raw bytes. Verify against the configured secret without printing it; reject invalid/stale signatures, deduplicate event IDs, reject stale versions and reconcile missing events through status queries. Sender delivery and consumer processing are separate. No real secret or account exists in this fixture.
